Nothing was left to do. The previous attempt had already committed the whole task as eda208f2, and I found no uncommitted changes. I re-ran the checks on that commit: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings and cargo test all pass (36 test result blocks, no failures). I didn't make a new commit.

What eda208f2 does:
• One table for Gemini limits. GOOGLE_PUBLISHED_LIMITS in src/providers.rs has a row for each of the 6 offered Gemini ids that have no yoagent preset. Each row is a 1,048,576-token window and 65,536-token output, read on 2026-11-08 from that model's own Google page, with the page's URL in the row. The ticket said 7 ids, but gemini-3.1-pro-preview already has a yoagent preset, so it needs no row. No offered id is still running on guessed limits.
• The run uses the table. The Google path in src/agent_builder.rs applies the row only when yoagent has no preset. A user's own max_tokens still wins, and a test pins that.
• `/model info` uses the same table. It now reads its window and an Output: line from the same place, and the old hand-typed number is gone. An unlisted Gemini id now shows "unknown" instead of a guessed 1M.
• Tests and probe. The new tests are in src/google_limits_tests.rs. They walk the offered Google list, so every id must have either a preset or a row, never both. The positive control worked: deleting the gemini-2.5-pro row made the first test fail by name, and it passed again once the row was back. In the built-binary probe, gemini-2.5-pro printed no guessed-limits warning and gemini-zzz still did.

One correction to the ticket, checked only by reading yoagent 0.27.4's code, not with a real request: the 8192 guess never actually capped Google replies. yoagent's Google provider sends the output limit only from the user's own --max-tokens. What the guess really affected was yoyo's context budget, the warning, the max-tokens ceiling check and /model info.

One thing remains wrong. The warning for unknown Gemini ids still says replies are "capped at 8192", which by that reading is false for Google. It's filed separately as #1158, because this push closes #1157.

